Note the `SPURIOUS-OTHER-DAY` (Jan 13) row is excluded — day-filter works.

### V4. Write path — 201 + read-back (with a stub endpoint)
```bash
node dist/cli.js consolidate --target 2026-01-14 --namespaces-root /tmp/ns \
  --write-digest DUCKBRAIN_API_KEY=stub DUCKBRAIN_API_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:8787
# expect: HTTP 201 verified, read-back 200 + digest match, output ends with
# [written to API: 201 verified]
```

V5. Confirm no regression on the API-driven tests that genuinely need the real key under
cron (`act`/CI): they still receive the key because `afterEach` restores it exactly.

